GPL-3.0-or-later, to parse and validate read-only SQL.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party software used by the core (Python)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Installed from PyPI as dependencies, not vendored. Versions are pinned in
uv.lock. Each package's own license text ships with the package.

  pglast            GPL-3.0-or-later   PostgreSQL parser bindings (embeds
                                       libpg_query, BSD-3-Clause, built from
                                       PostgreSQL sources, PostgreSQL License)
  psycopg,          LGPL-3.0-only      PostgreSQL driver and connection pool
  psycopg-pool
  psycopg-binary    LGPL-3.0-only      binary wheel; bundles libpq
                                       (PostgreSQL License) and OpenSSL
                                       (Apache-2.0)
  fastapi           MIT
  starlette         BSD-3-Clause
  uvicorn           BSD-3-Clause
  pydantic,         MIT
  pydantic-core
  typer             MIT
  click             BSD-3-Clause
  rich              MIT
  httpx             BSD-3-Clause
  anyio             MIT

Optional extra "images":

  pillow            MIT-CMU (HPND)
  pillow-heif       BSD-3-Clause; its binary wheels bundle libheif and
                    libde265 (LGPL-3.0) and x265 (GPL-2.0-or-later)

The Docker image additionally contains Debian packages (postgresql-client,
gnupg, zstd, rsync, openssh-client, ffmpeg and their dependencies) under
their own licenses, listed in /usr/share/doc/*/copyright inside the image.

